cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this helped, cite it."
type: software
title: "One network pass matches turbulence's statistics. The vortices are missing"
abstract: "One evaluation of a small network turns noise into a field of two-dimensional Kolmogorov turbulence whose energy spectrum is within 1.5% of a pseudo-spectral solver's at every scale down to the dissipation scale and whose vorticity distribution is within 5% down to 1/10,000 of its peak, at an estimated 3,700 times lower GPU cost. The fields have none of the flow's structure: the alignment of vorticity gradients with the strain is 0.01 against the solver's 0.41. With the measurement that shows it, a dynamical test, and a network-free semi-Lagrangian step that keeps two-time correlations and velocity differences within tolerance over 1,000 turnover times where a learned step fails."
authors:
  - family-names: Bogdan
    given-names: Philipp
